
F. WHAT COUNTS AS THE AGENT CLOSING THE CONVERSATION
  [PASS] F1. a sign-off the agent ends its turn on closes the call
  [PASS] F2. a closing phrase used MID-CONVERSATION does not close the call
  [PASS] F3. a turn that still asks something is a handover point, never an ending
  [PASS] F4. an ordinary courtesy is not a sign-off
  [PASS] F5. the last turn must be the AGENT's — a talking caller is never cut off
  [PASS] F6. an agent-only transcript never closes a call

G. A CLOSING WITH A TRAILING VOCATIVE (THE REPORTED DEFECT)
